    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2MGG2yV7DSNFc1bcB527HGo)_\n\n## What was wrong\n- Stacking is `join-with`, which only existed in AeroSpace's service mode as plain `shift-h/j/k/l`.\n- After `Caps+Shift+;`, Caps Lock is usually still held, so Hammerspoon's layer takes `Shift+h/j/k/l` as *move window* first. Both tools then compete for the same chord, so joining only works sometimes (when Caps is released first).\n\n## Fix\n- `Caps+Ctrl+h/j/k/l` runs `aerospace join-with <dir>` directly on the layer, with no service mode.\n- The layer key is also bound with Ctrl, so Ctrl-then-Caps works.\n- `aerospace.org` documents the new keys. The service-mode keys are unchanged.\n\n## Testing (not run: no Mac in the container)\n- Reload Hammerspoon, open two tiled windows side by side, press `Caps+Ctrl+l`/`h`: they should join into one container (then `Caps+,` for accordion).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBGFAv6aqFgYu7ykH3)_",
